{=============================================================================
  Evaporative condenser as a semi-isothermal exchanger (exercise)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0227
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Nominal conditions of an evaporative condenser treated as a
  semi-isothermal exchanger. The air-side heat rate sets the capacity
  rate C_dot_a_f from the inlet and outlet wet-bulb temperatures. The
  effectiveness, the NTU and AU_f then follow. The exchange coefficient
  is assumed constant. Teaching exercise of ULiège MSTh, repetition 5,
  exercise 3 (continued), not an exam. Humid air: no diagram-state arrays.

  Inputs : Q_dot_cd, T_a_su, T_a_ex, P_a, RH_su, RH_ex, T_cd
  Outputs: C_dot_a_f, T_wb_su, T_wb_ex, epsilon_cd, NTU_f, AU_f
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège MSTh, R5 - SB - Ex 3.EES, Stéphane Bertagnolio
           - see README.md
  Licence: MIT. Status: verified against the EES stored solution.
=============================================================================}

"MSTh - SB - R5 - Exercice 3 (suite)"

"!Nominal conditions"
Q_dot_cd = 35000          "condenser heat rate [W]"
T_a_su = 25               "inlet air dry-bulb temperature [C]"
T_a_ex = 30               "outlet air dry-bulb temperature [C]"
P_a = 101325              "air pressure [Pa]"
RH_su = 0.6               "inlet air relative humidity [-]"
RH_ex = 1                 "outlet air relative humidity [-]"
T_cd = 45                 "condenser temperature [C]"

"A semi-isothermal exchanger is assumed, as in the original."

"!Air side"
Q_dot_cd = C_dot_a_f*(T_wb_ex - T_wb_su)                              "air-side heat rate [W]"
T_wb_su = WETBULB(AirH2O, T=T_a_su, P=P_a, R=RH_su)                   "inlet wet-bulb temperature [C]"
T_wb_ex = WETBULB(AirH2O, T=T_a_ex, P=P_a, R=RH_ex)                   "outlet wet-bulb temperature [C]"

"!Effectiveness of the evaporative condenser"
Q_dot_cd = epsilon_cd*C_dot_a_f*(T_cd - T_wb_su)                      "heat rate from the effectiveness [W]"

epsilon_cd = 1 - exp(-NTU_f)                                          "evaporative-condenser effectiveness [-]"
NTU_f = AU_f/C_dot_a_f                                                "number of transfer units [-]"

"One obtains, as in the original:"
"AU_f = 1767"    "exchange coefficient assumed constant; stored result, not an equation"
